# Both calls have same-sign exponents separated by p.  The SE domain cannot
# distinguish their mantissas, so each result represents SE-S1's identity and
# rounded alternatives.
%3#0 is {(s = +, e = 0), (s = +, e = 1)}
%3#1 is {(s = -, e = -47)
%3#1 is {(s = ±, e = -24)}
%4#0 is {(s = +, e = 0), (s = +, e = 1)}
%4#1 is {(s = -, e = -47)
%4#1 is {(s = ±, e = -24)}
